(gen_random_uuid(), 'taylor-swift-seahawks-end-game-friendship-bracelet-backlash-20261028', 'taylor-swift', 'United States',
'Seahawks Mocked Taylor Swift With ''End Game'' Bracelets — and Swifties Hit Back After 20-3 Chiefs Win',
'',
'The Seattle Seahawks mocked Taylor Swift with an ''End Game'' friendship-bracelet post after their 20-3 win over the Kansas City Chiefs on 25 October 2026, and by 27 October 2026 the joke had turned into a full-blown fan row.',
'',
$$<p>The Seattle Seahawks mocked Taylor Swift with an "End Game" friendship-bracelet post after beating the Kansas City Chiefs 20-3 on 25 October 2026 — and by 27 October 2026 the joke had turned into a full-blown fan row, with Swifties accusing the team of taking a cheap shot at a player's wife. The backlash, first flagged by TMZ and then picked up across outlets, is now the week's loudest Taylor Swift talking point: a victory celebration that became an argument about where trolling ends and disrespect begins.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Game</th><td>Seahawks 20, Chiefs 3 — 25 October 2026, Lumen Field, Seattle</td></tr>
<tr><th>The post</th><td>Bracelets spelling "Seahawks Win", captioned "End Game"</td></tr>
<tr><th>Second post</th><td>Mascot Blitz post captioned "Lately, I've been dressin' for revenge"</td></tr>
<tr><th>Why it stung</th><td>"End Game" is from Swift's 2017 album "reputation"; bracelets are a Swiftie tradition</td></tr>
<tr><th>Fan reaction</th><td>Swifties called the posts "classless"; other fans called them funny</td></tr>
<tr><th>Swift's whereabouts</th><td>In Nashville on 26 October 2026, not Seattle</td></tr>
<tr><th>Response so far</th><td>Neither Swift nor Kelce has addressed the posts publicly</td></tr>
<tr><th>What is next</th><td>Chiefs at Broncos on 1 November 2026; Seahawks host Bears on 2 November 2026</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>The post that started it</h2>
<p>Shortly after the final whistle, the Seahawks' official account shared a photo of two friendship bracelets in white, blue and green beads spelling out "Seahawks Win", <a href="https://trending.thespun.com/trending/seahawks-backlash-taylor-swift-fans-chiefs">The Spun reported</a>. The caption was two words: "End Game". <a href="https://www.the-sun.com/sport/17214284/seattle-seahawks-blasted-swifties-mocked-travis-kelce-post/">The Sun</a>, which also covered the post, described it as beaded bracelets posted to Instagram, with the caption alluding to Swift's 2017 hit. The team did not stop there: <a href="https://www.essentiallysports.com/nfl-active-news-seahawks-mock-travis-kelce-taylor-swift-after-win-over-chiefs/">EssentiallySports reported</a> a second post from mascot Blitz, shown in a shimmering concert-style outfit, captioned "Lately, I've been dressin' for revenge", a line the outlet identified as a reference to Swift's song "Vigilante Shit". <a href="https://www.thehollywoodgossip.com/taylor-swift-fans-furious-at-seattle-seahawks-over-friendship-bracelet-meme/">The Hollywood Gossip</a> likewise noted the bracelet was not the team's only Swift nod.</p>
<h2>Why the Seahawks mocked Taylor Swift post hit a nerve</h2>
<p>Friendship bracelets are not a random prop. They have become closely associated with Swift's fan community during her Eras Tour, when fans traded handmade bracelets at concerts, The Spun reported. The tradition is partly inspired by her song "You're on Your Own, Kid" from her 2022 album "Midnights", which includes the lyric "So make the friendship bracelets, take the moment and taste it". The bracelets are also woven into the couple's own story: before they began dating, Kelce tried to give Swift a bracelet bearing his phone number during her 2023 Eras Tour stop in Kansas City, The Spun reported. He never delivered it, but the two began dating and married in July 2026. That is why the post landed: it borrowed the fandom's own symbol and pointed it at its idol after her husband's team had lost.</p>
<h2>The game behind the troll</h2>
<p>The football was one-sided. The reigning Super Bowl champion Seahawks dominated defensively at Lumen Field, The Spun reported, limiting Kansas City to three points and 213 total yards. The Chiefs never entered the red zone, and their only points came from a 50-yard Harrison Butker field goal, The Sun reported. The defeat ended Kansas City's unbeaten start to the 2026 season, leaving the Chiefs at 5-1, and Kelce finished with four catches for 44 yards. <a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/us/nfl/seattle-seahawks-troll-taylor-swift-and-travis-kelce-after-beating-kansas-city-chiefs-12238822">NDTV Sports</a> reported on 26 October 2026 that Seattle had handed the Chiefs their first loss of the season, and the social media team had then "found a way to bring Taylor Swift into the conversation". The win was emphatic; the argument is about what came after.</p>
<h2>Swifties split: fury, and laughter</h2>
<p>The angry reaction was swift. "Be better. That's beneath you to go after a player's wife," one fan wrote, The Sun reported. The Spun collected more of the same: one commenter asked why trolling "the spouse of an opposing player" was acceptable "if she wasn't Taylor Swift", and another said: "What other players wife would you make fun of? I thought your organization was better than that. Disrespectful and tasteless." Then came the warnings. "Karma will get you. Leave Taylor out if this," one fan wrote, The Spun reported, while another warned: "Btw, Tayvoodoo will find you. Say goodbye to your SB chances." The so-called "Swiftie Curse" ran through much of the backlash, The Spun reported. Other fans, though, refused to be offended on Swift's behalf. "I'm a huge Swiftie and I cannot believe people are getting so worked up about it. I thought it was funny," one fan posted, The Sun reported. Some fans cheered the admin instead, The Hollywood Gossip reported.</p>
<h2>Where was Swift?</h2>
<p>Part of what annoyed fans, The Hollywood Gossip reported, is that Swift was not even in the building: she did not appear to make the trip to Seattle. The explanation is happier: on 26 October 2026, the day after the game, Swift was in Nashville being inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame as its youngest-ever member, as covered in <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/taylor-swift-nashville-songwriters-hall-of-fame-induction-20261027">our report on the induction</a>. At the same gala she had laughed off a prank in public, joking about Brad Paisley filling her tour bus with live crickets in 2007, as covered in <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/taylor-swift-brad-paisley-crickets-tour-bus-prank-20261027">our report on the crickets prank</a>. That joke was hers to tell, on her own night; the Seahawks' version was told about her, without her, after a defeat.</p>
<h2>What to watch next</h2>
<p>Three things will decide how long this row runs. The first is the response, or the lack of one: neither Swift nor Kelce has publicly addressed the bracelet posts, The Hollywood Gossip reported, with no reporting that the posts have been taken down. The second is the scoreboard: the Chiefs travel to face the Denver Broncos on 1 November 2026, while the Seahawks host the Chicago Bears on 2 November 2026, The Sun reported. The third is the precedent: this post dragged a player's wife into it, and the reaction may make the next social media team think twice.</p>$$,
